where $\phi_k(x, y)$ is the $k$-th element of $\Phi(x, y)$, $\theta_1, \theta_2, \ldots, \theta_{d/2}$ are frequency weights, and $\theta_k = 10000^{-2k/d}$. Context: $\Phi(x, y) = W_{\Phi}(x||y)$ through a learnable linear transformation, where $||$ denotes vector concatenation and $W_{\Phi} \in \mathbb{R}^{d/2 \times 2}$ is a learnable projection matrix.
